<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <PackageId>ModelHub.MultiTenancy.EntityFrameworkCore</PackageId>
    <Description>EF Core support for ModelHub.MultiTenancy. It keeps every query and every save inside the current tenant, so a forgotten Where clause can't leak one customer's data to another.

What it adds:
• ApplyTenantQueryFilters(): one call in OnModelCreating adds a tenant filter to every entity that implements ITenantEntity. A request with no tenant sees no tenant rows. Works alongside your own filters such as soft delete (a named filter on EF Core 10, combined on EF Core 8).
• UseMultiTenancy(): a save interceptor that stamps the current tenant on new rows and refuses any insert, update, delete or tenant change that touches another tenant's data (TenantMismatchException).
• WhereVisibleToSubTenants(): limits a query to the user's sub-tenants, such as branches, sites or departments.

Example: a veterinary practice SaaS
VetDesk sells practice-management software. Each practice group is a tenant and each clinic is a sub-tenant. Northfield Vets (clinics in Leeds and York) and Riverside Animal Care share one database.
– A developer writes db.Appointments.ToListAsync() and forgets the practice filter. Without this package, Northfield's staff would see Riverside's clients and pets. With it, the query returns Northfield's rows only.
– A receptionist at the York clinic sees York's appointments only; Northfield's practice manager sees both clinics.
– A faulty import, running as Northfield, tries to save a pet record stamped with Riverside's tenant id. The save is refused before anything reaches the database.
– A VetDesk support engineer acts as Northfield to investigate a ticket. They see exactly what Northfield sees, nothing more, and the access is logged.

Targets .NET 8 (EF Core 8) and .NET 10 (EF Core 10). Use with ModelHub.MultiTenancy, which resolves the tenant from the signed-in user's token.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\ModelHub.MultiTenancy\ModelHub.MultiTenancy.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="8.0.23" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="10.0.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
